@{ ViewData["Title"] = "Reports"; }
@using SupplyChain.Application.Reports.TransactionStatement

<h1 class="h4 mb-1">Reports</h1>
<p class="text-body-secondary">
    Replaces the legacy Reports menu. Fifty-six Crystal report files are being consolidated into
    roughly twenty parameterised reports &mdash; see <code>docs/05-Reporting-Strategy.md</code>.
</p>

<div class="row row-cols-1 row-cols-md-2 g-3 mt-1">
    <div class="col">
        <div class="card h-100">
            <div class="card-header fw-semibold">Supply Chain</div>
            <div class="list-group list-group-flush">
                <a class="list-group-item list-group-item-action"
                   asp-action="TransactionStatement" asp-route-mode="@StatementFilterMode.BillNo">
                    Bill Wise Report
                    <small class="d-block text-body-secondary">Statement lines for one bill number</small>
                </a>
                <a class="list-group-item list-group-item-action"
                   asp-action="TransactionStatement" asp-route-mode="@StatementFilterMode.MrrNo">
                    MRR Wise Report
                    <small class="d-block text-body-secondary">Statement lines for one goods receipt</small>
                </a>
                <a class="list-group-item list-group-item-action"
                   asp-action="TransactionStatement" asp-route-mode="@StatementFilterMode.ChallanNo">
                    Challan Wise Report
                    <small class="d-block text-body-secondary">Statement lines for one challan</small>
                </a>
                <a class="list-group-item list-group-item-action"
                   asp-action="TransactionStatement" asp-route-mode="@StatementFilterMode.Transaction">
                    Transaction Wise Report
                    <small class="d-block text-body-secondary">By date range, type and statement number</small>
                </a>
                <a class="list-group-item list-group-item-action" asp-action="PartyStatement">
                    Party Statement
                    <small class="d-block text-body-secondary">Detail or summary, by party and period</small>
                </a>
                <a class="list-group-item list-group-item-action" asp-action="MonthlyStatement">
                    Monthly Statement
                    <small class="d-block text-body-secondary">Totals by month and transaction type</small>
                </a>
                <a class="list-group-item list-group-item-action" asp-action="PurchaseOrderRegister">
                    Purchase Order Register
                    <small class="d-block text-body-secondary">By order, supplier or item type</small>
                </a>
                <a class="list-group-item list-group-item-action" asp-action="MrrRegister">
                    Goods Receipt Register
                    <small class="d-block text-body-secondary">Six filter modes, MRR or challan</small>
                </a>
                <a class="list-group-item list-group-item-action" asp-action="ItemMovement">
                    Item Movement
                    <small class="d-block text-body-secondary">Ordered against received, per item</small>
                </a>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="col">
        <div class="card h-100">
            <div class="card-header fw-semibold">Accounts &amp; Store</div>
            <div class="list-group list-group-flush">
                <a class="list-group-item list-group-item-action" asp-action="BillRegister">
                    Bill Register
                    <small class="d-block text-body-secondary">Eight filter modes, cash or credit</small>
                </a>
                <a class="list-group-item list-group-item-action" asp-action="ChequeRegister">
                    Cheque Register
                    <small class="d-block text-body-secondary">By book, issue date or beneficiary</small>
                </a>
                <a class="list-group-item list-group-item-action" asp-controller="Mrrs" asp-action="Balance">
                    PO &amp; MRR Balance Qty
                    <small class="d-block text-body-secondary">Ordered against received</small>
                </a>
                <a class="list-group-item list-group-item-action" asp-action="Audit">
                    Audit Report
                    <small class="d-block text-body-secondary">Who created, changed or deleted a document</small>
                </a>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="alert alert-light border small mt-3 d-flex align-items-start gap-2">
    <span>ℹ️</span>
    <div>
        <strong>Fifty-six Crystal report files become eleven parameterised reports.</strong> The
        legacy system needed one <code>.rpt</code> per filter combination and per currency; a
        modern report takes its parameters at runtime. The Bill Register alone replaces sixteen
        files; the Purchase Order Register replaces thirteen. Every report family turned out to be
        one query with parameters. See <code>docs/05-Reporting-Strategy.md</code> §6.
    </div>
</div>
